"# Detailed description of the target figure: `fig_intercept_error`\n\n## 1. Content and data mapping\n\n**Chart type:** Single-series point chart (scatter plot). No connecting line, no fitted or interpolated curve, no error bars, no confidence bands, and no additional points.\n\n**Variable-to-channel mapping:**\n\n| Channel | Variable | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| x-position | Added intercept correction *b* | Experimental log, column \"Added b\" |\n| y-position | Mean squared error (MSE) | Experimental log, column \"Mean squared error\" |\n| Color (hue) | None; one series | n/a |\n| Shape | Filled circle for all points | n/a |\n| Text label | MSE value at each point | Same MSE value, formatted as shown below |\n\n**Every measured point, enumerated:**\n\n| Point | x = b | y = MSE | Point label |\n|---|---:|---:|---|\n| P1 | 0 | 9 | \"MSE = 9\" |\n| P2 | 1.5 | 2.25 | \"MSE = 2.25\" |\n| P3 | 3 | 0 | \"MSE = 0\" |\n\n**Consistency check against the log:** The residuals of the baseline (2x) are y \u2212 2x = 3 for all five observations, so MSE(b=0) = 3\u00b2 = 9. For b = 1.5, each residual is 3 \u2212 1.5 = 1.5, so MSE = 2.25. For b = 3, each residual is 0, so MSE = 0. These match the recorded values. The correction b = 3 is the mean of y \u2212 2x and is also the value that drives MSE to zero on these same five observations.\n\n**Scope statement:** This figure shows only arithmetic error reduction on the five observations used to determine the correction. It makes no claim about generalization, timing, or held-out performance. The subtitle or caption must say so.\n\n## 2. Text content\n\n- **Title:** \"Measured Mean Squared Error at Three Intercept Corrections\"\n- **x-axis title:** \"Added intercept correction *b*\" (unitless)\n- **y-axis title:** \"Mean squared error (MSE)\" (unitless)\n- **Caption (bottom left, below the plot):** \"Each point is one deterministic evaluation on the same five observations used to determine b. No uncertainty is shown.\"\n\n## 3. Axis specification\n\n- **x-axis:** Limits `c(-0.25, 3.25)`. Breaks at `c(0, 1.5, 3)`, labeled \"0\", \"1.5\", \"3\".\n- **y-axis:** Limits `c(-0.5, 10)`, so the point at MSE = 0 is not clipped at the axis. Breaks at `seq(0, 10, by = 2)`.\n- **Axis lines:** Left and bottom axis lines, 0.5 pt, color `#444444`.\n- **Tick marks:** Length 3 pt, color `#444444`.\n\n## 4. Aesthetic specification\n\n**Colors:**\n\n| Element | HEX |\n|---|---|\n| Background (panel and plot) | `#FFFFFF` |\n| Major gridlines | `#E3E3E3` |\n| Minor gridlines | None |\n| Markers (fill) | `#1F4E79` |\n| Marker outline | `#FFFFFF`, 0.6 pt |\n| Title text | `#1A1A1A` |\n| Axis titles | `#333333` |\n| Tick labels | `#444444` |\n| Point labels | `#1F4E79` |\n| Caption | `#666666` |\n\n**Typography (sans-serif, e.g., Helvetica or Arial):**\n\n| Element | Size | Weight |\n|---|---|---|\n| Title | 14 pt | Bold |\n| Axis titles | 12 pt | Regular |\n| Tick labels | 10 pt | Regular |\n| Point labels | 10 pt | Regular |\n| Caption | 9 pt | Italic |\n\n**Markers:**\n\n- Shape: filled circle (ggplot2 `shape = 21`, fill `#1F4E79`, stroke white).\n- Size: `size = 4` (about 4 mm in ggplot2 units).\n- Stroke width: 0.6 pt.\n\n**Point labels:**\n\n- Position: placed above each point and horizontally centered (`vjust = -1.1`, `hjust = 0.5`).\n- Text: the MSE value as shown in the table above.\n\n**Gridlines:**\n\n- Major gridlines on the y-axis only, 0.4 pt, `#E3E3E3`.\n- Vertical gridlines at the three b values, 0.3 pt, `#E3E3E3`, dashed (`linetype = \"dashed\"`), to aid reading of the x positions.\n\n**Legend:** None. There is one series, and the labels carry the values.\n\n**Plot dimensions:** 5.5 in wide by 4.0 in tall. Margins of 10 pt on all sides.\n\n## 5. Reproducible R/ggplot2 specification\n\nThe code must use only the three recorded pairs. It must not fit a model or add a line, smooth, or interpolation.\n\n```r\nlibrary(ggplot2)\n\ndf <- data.frame(\n  b   = c(0, 1.5, 3),\n  mse = c(9, 2.25, 0)\n)\n\np <- ggplot(df, aes(x = b, y = mse)) +\n  geom_vline(xintercept = df$b, colour = \"#E3E3E3\",\n             linewidth = 0.3, linetype = \"dashed\") +\n  geom_point(shape = 21, size = 4, fill = \"#1F4E79\",\n             colour = \"#FFFFFF\", stroke = 0.6) +\n  geom_text(aes(label = paste0(\"MSE = \", format(mse, drop0trailing = TRUE))),\n            vjust = -1.1, size = 3.5, colour = \"#1F4E79\") +\n  scale_x_continuous(limits = c(-0.25, 3.25), breaks = c(0, 1.5, 3)) +\n  scale_y_continuous(limits = c(-0.5, 10), breaks = seq(0, 10, by = 2)) +\n  labs(\n    title   = \"Measured Mean Squared Error at Three Intercept Corrections\",\n    x       = \"Added intercept correction b\",\n    y       = \"Mean squared error (MSE)\",\n    caption = \"Each point is one deterministic evaluation on the same five observations used to determine b. No uncertainty is shown.\"\n  ) +\n  theme_minimal(base_family = \"Helvetica\") +\n  theme(\n    plot.background   = element_rect(fill = \"#FFFFFF\", colour = NA),\n    panel.background  = element_rect(fill = \"#FFFFFF\", colour = NA),\n    panel.grid.major.x = element_blank(),\n    panel.grid.minor  = element_blank(),\n    panel.grid.major.y = element_line(colour = \"#E3E3E3\", linewidth = 0.4),\n    axis.line         = element_line(colour = \"#444444\", linewidth = 0.5),\n    axis.ticks        = element_line(colour = \"#444444\"),\n    axis.ticks.length = unit(3, \"pt\"),\n    plot.title        = element_text(size = 14, face = \"bold\", colour = \"#1A1A1A\"),\n    axis.title        = element_text(size = 12, colour = \"#333333\"),\n    axis.text         = element_text(size = 10, colour = \"#444444\"),\n    plot.caption      = element_text(size = 9, face = \"italic\", colour = \"#666666\", hjust = 0),\n    legend.position   = \"none\",\n    plot.margin       = margin(10, 10, 10, 10, \"pt\")\n  )\n```\n\n**Output artifacts (to be produced by the downstream step, which keeps these as separate reproducibility files):**\n\n1. Editable R source: `fig_intercept_error.R`, containing the code above.\n2. Vector PDF: `fig_intercept_error.pdf`, saved with `ggsave(..., width = 5.5, height = 4.0, device = cairo_pdf)`.\n3. Manuscript-compatible preview: `fig_intercept_error.png`, saved at 300 dpi with the same dimensions."